<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Madagascar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1942">1942</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a> was the Allied campaign of 1942 to take <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vichy">Vichy</a> French Madagascar and deny its harbours to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>. British forces landed near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antsiranana">Diego Suarez</a> on 5 May 1942 and captured the naval base, then advanced on the rest of the island from September. The Vichy governor-general surrendered in November, and the island was handed over to the Free French.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-madagascar.jpg" alt="Battle of Madagascar" width="320" height="237" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: British Official Photographer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Madagascar_KAR_1942.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
